                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.60F8/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Chapin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Praha</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-06-07T15:00:00+01:00">June 7, 1937—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 7—1:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>31. Your No. 10, April 13, 1 p.m. Practice of issuance of certificates based upon
                    local legislation. Foreign Office states that situation is being studied by
                    Council of Ministers and that means are being sought to meet Treasury
                    representation by Ministerial decree with consideration to application of law to
                    other countries. Hope is expressed that Treasury will not make declaration of
                    bounty pending study here which I am assured will be expedited.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chapin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
